**Veterans' Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI)** is a specialized life insurance product offered by the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs that provides mortgage protection specifically for veterans with severe service-connected disabilities who have adapted their homes to meet their needs. Unlike standard group policies, VMLI guarantees payment of your outstanding home mortgage balance directly to the bank or lender holding your loan.

Here is everything you need to know about qualifying for this program and managing your coverage once you receive it:

### 1. How To Get Qualification
To be eligible for **Voters Mortgage Life Insurance (VMLI)**, you must meet all of the following requirements at the same time [p716]:
*   You must have a severe disability that was caused or made worse by your military service;
*   You must receive a **Specially Adapted Housing (SAH)** grant to buy, build, or make changes to your home so you can live independently;
*   You must be the legal owner (holder of the title) and have an active mortgage on that home;
*   You must still be under **70 years old** at the time of application.

